was found in its subtree (or None). If both children return non-null, the current node is where the paths split: the LCA. Otherwise propagate the non-null result upward. For a BST, compare values and walk down instead: O(h).</p>","python":"def lowest_common_ancestor(root, p, q):\n    def go(n):\n        if not n or n.val in (p, q):\n            return n\n        l, r = go(n.left), go(n.right)\n        return n if l and r else (l or r)\n    return go(root).val\n","cpp":"TreeNode* go_(TreeNode* n, int p, int q) { if (!n || n->val == p || n->val == q) return n; auto l = go_(n->left, p, q), r = go_(n->right, p, q); return l && r ? n : (l ? l : r); }\nint lowestCommonAncestor(TreeNode* root, int p, int q) { return go_(root, p, q)->val; }\n"},"arg_kinds":["tree",null,null],"ret_kind":null}